mit/5889d1b161cfcad8e8183b79cf67cbccf005e546","commit_subject":"Windows VPN plug-in app and host: VpnHoodWindowsVpnPluginApp, the app in the window's process with its storage and lock in the package's LocalState, its own device UI provider and a tunnel that outlives it; WindowsVpnPluginDesktopHost, the head's entry point over InProcessDesktopHost, logging to LocalState\\window.log from its first line and naming its window by the app id. Neither references AppLib.App.Windows nor Hosting.Desktop.Windows, so no WinTun or WinDivert comes along. The five projects join the solution (the component as x64) and the source layout's trees","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"MahjongPantheon/pantheon","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-22T20:55:15Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"eca68d80836c82aeb8bfb5fa44831834c403f57b","github_link":"https://github.com/MahjongPantheon/pantheon/commit/eca68d80836c82aeb8bfb5fa44831834c403f57b","commit_subject":"[codex] Rewrite Hugin monitoring service in TypeScript","ai_tool":"Codex"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-22T20:55:14Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"c7c5aeb2fe4c951f45afdc5d17180b2d0ba417c0","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/c7c5aeb2fe4c951f45afdc5d17180b2d0ba417c0","commit_subject":"Desktop: the window without a service - InProcessDesktopHost runs the app and its window in one process as a host's whole job, for a desktop whose tunnel the OS holds (the Windows VPN plug-in): the window's single-instance claim, then the app, then the window over its loopback API, and a failure as the UI's one message. \"dev\" runs the same window. The window takes only its share of the paths (IDesktopUiPaths, which IAppDesktopPaths extends), and the in-process connection no instance controller","ai_tool":"Claude"}]